KZ2 patch 2165: measure ZPASS occlusion counts on the Metal draw engine (light coronas).

Written for the Pyrrhus native Mac lighting work. The slot-per-draw visibility buffer, the
query/ticket ranges and CLEAR_REPORT_VALUE handling follow the author's Resistance 3 macOS
port (rsx_draw_engine_zpass_*, eng_set_occlusion, MIT, Erik Martins); the per-commit buffer,
the completion-handler harvest and the never-waiting report path are new here. No RPCS3 code.
On Metal every GET_REPORT(ZPASS_PIXEL_CNT) answered 0xFFFF ("visible"): only the D3D12 live
draw measured it (KZ3 patch 2027). Killzone 2 sizes and fades its light coronas by these
counts, so on the Mac every corona showed as a hard dot at full strength, through walls.
Now each counted draw gets a slot in its commit's MTLVisibilityResultModeCounting buffer; the
command buffer's completion handler sums them per query; the report is answered at once with
the last count its area received and the real count is written there once the GPU is done
(the title reads it a frame later, as with 2027). Nothing waits on the GPU.
PS3RECOMP_ENG_ZPASS=0 restores the constant answer; GCM_ZPASS_LOG=<n> prints the first counts.

